  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CN})_4\\right]^{2-}$ is square planar, diamagnetic $(0$ unpaired electrons) with $d s p^2$ hybridisation. \n$\\left[\\mathrm{Ni}(\\mathrm{CO})_4\\right]$ - is tetrahedral,diamagnetic ( $0$ unpaired electrons) with $s p^3$ hybridisation. \n$\\left[\\mathrm{NiCl}_4\\right]^{2-}$ is tetrahedral, paramagnetic ($2$ unpaired electrons) with $s p^3$ hybridisation. \nHence, the option (c) is the correct answer.",
